  "bounded_findings": [
    "With identical deployment parameters the newer model commands greater knee flexion, already on flat ground.",
    "Both models traverse the 6cm and 10cm isolated platforms without triggering the fall criterion.",
    "On five 15cm-rise/28cm-tread stairs, 37500 stays upright and reaches the landing; 2000 triggers the fall criterion.",
    "On the 12-step 1.4m-wide stair, lateral foot placement crosses the stair/landing edge before large tilt and collapse. At t=9.38s pelvis y=-0.701m and left ankle y=-0.750m, while torso up cosine remains 0.997.",
    "A width-only change to 2.8m with the same PD permits 37500 to reach x>5.5m on the upper landing without triggering the fall criterion. Lateral drift persists.",
    "Knees do not reach the 300Nm cap in the latest-model stair cases. This alone does not exclude finite PD compliance or tracking lag.",
    "Ankle pitch torque clipping is present on stairs, but no causal intervention on that cap was performed; clipping cannot by itself identify the failure cause.",
    "The latest model exports no embedded metadata and currently reuses the supplied 1500 contract. Matching tensor dimensions does not prove PD/default pose/action scales/observation conventions match the 37500 training run."
